// Solar Weather Clock — custom firmware for Logan's build (gift for Mia)
//
// Board: ESP32-C3 SuperMini · OLED 0.96" SSD1306 (0x3C) · SHT31 (0x44)
// SDA=GPIO4  SCL=GPIO5
//
// WHAT THIS DOES
//  1. Boot: "Connecting To Earth..." flashes on screen while Wi-Fi connects
//     and the first weather/time fetch completes.
//  2. Once real data is loaded for the first time: a one-time welcome
//     message for Mia, then it settles into the main clock.
//  3. Main screen ("blanket" view): time, date, indoor temp/humidity, and
//     outdoor weather all visible together, all the time.
//  4. Every 5 minutes: one of your messages takes over the whole screen for
//     a few seconds, word-wrapped across as many lines as it needs, then
//     back to normal.
//  5. Every hour: a special full-screen moment (Mars-and-back, a shooting
//     star, a weather-reactive scene, or — rarely — the proposal screen).
//
// EDIT HERE — your messages are down in the MESSAGES[] block below. Add as
// many as you want (no fixed limit other than the ESP32's flash size, which
// easily holds hundreds of short strings).

